  "notes": "しゃぶる means to put something in the mouth and suck, lick, or gnaw on it. It is colloquial and often used in the context of babies, children, or animals.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を for the thing being sucked\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {指|ゆび}をしゃぶる: to suck one's finger (babies/children)\n- {骨|ほね}をしゃぶる: to chew/gnaw on a bone\n- あめをしゃぶる: to suck on candy\n- おしゃぶり: pacifier (derived noun)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {舐|な}める: to lick (more general, broader use)\n- {吸|す}う: to suck, to inhale (liquids, cigarettes, air)\n\nIDIOM:\n{骨|ほね}までしゃぶる means to exploit someone to the bone, squeezing out every last bit of value.",
